1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Hi - this is the ComplianceIQ capstone demo.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:18,000
ComplianceIQ is an AI-driven multi-agent regulatory compliance system.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It reads internal policies, compares them against IRDAI / MAS regulations,

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,000
identifies compliance gaps, scores them by severity, and produces an audit-ready DOCX report.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
End to end in under 30 minutes for less than $0.10 in OpenAI usage.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The problem: compliance teams spend weeks each quarter cross-referencing policies.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Multi-jurisdiction complexity - IRDAI and MAS update constantly.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Mapping is manual - tens of thousands of clause connections done by hand.

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Gaps surface during the audit, not before.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Documentation burden - evidence binders rebuilt every cycle.

11
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:45,000
ComplianceIQ replaces all of this with an observable, reproducible AI pipeline.

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,571
Architecture - five logical layers.

13
00:01:53,571 --> 00:02:02,143
L1 Ingestion: PDFs/DOCX in, classified chunks out.

14
00:02:02,143 --> 00:02:10,714
L2 Vector store: ChromaDB + OpenAI embeddings.

15
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:19,286
L3 Agents: Regulation Monitor, Gap Detector, Policy Analyzer.

16
00:02:19,286 --> 00:02:27,857
L4 Orchestration: workflow + scoring + evidence + remediation.

17
00:02:27,857 --> 00:02:36,429
L5 Interfaces: knowledge graph, DOCX, Gradio dashboard, FastAPI.

18
00:02:36,429 --> 00:02:45,000
Cross-cutting Langfuse observability + immutable audit log on every run.

19
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:56,250
12-stage data flow with JSONL contracts at every stage.

20
00:02:56,250 --> 00:03:07,500
Each stage is independently runnable and re-runnable.

21
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:18,750
Re-runs are idempotent - Chroma uses deterministic IDs.

22
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:30,000
Every LLM-bearing stage is traced in Langfuse.

23
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Three specialized agents - single-responsibility, LCEL, Pydantic-typed.

24
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Regulation Monitor: extracts mandatory actions and evidence needs per file.

25
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Gap Detector: top-5 RAG over policy chunks; LLM judges coverage + confidence.

26
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Policy Analyzer: aggregates gaps per Domain into weighted CoverageAssessment.

27
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Every agent: prompt | llm.with_structured_output(schema). Schema violations fail fast.

28
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:51,000
LIVE DEMO segment.

29
00:04:51,000 --> 00:05:12,000
TERMINAL: python main.py orchestrate --concurrency 8 --limit 5

30
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:33,000
(Watch the Regulation Monitor, then Gap Detector running in parallel.)

31
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Each gap is appended to gaps.jsonl in real time.

32
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:15,000
When done: type data\processed\compliance_score.json | more

33
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:36,000
The score is pure-Python deterministic - severity weights {3,2,1} x coverage {1.0, 0.5, 0.0}.

34
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Auditors can recompute by hand. Same gaps in => same score out.

35
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Now: python main.py dashboard => http://localhost:7860

36
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Click through Overview -> Gaps -> Coverage -> Remediation -> Search -> Reports.

37
00:07:39,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Then the Upload tab: file picker + HITL queue panel.

38
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:12,857
Key technical decisions.

39
00:08:12,857 --> 00:08:25,714
LCEL + Pydantic: schema violations fail at the agent boundary.

40
00:08:25,714 --> 00:08:38,571
Deterministic Python scoring - no LLM in the headline metric.

41
00:08:38,571 --> 00:08:51,429
JSONL contracts per stage - jq, pandas, Excel all 'just work'.

42
00:08:51,429 --> 00:09:04,286
Fail-open Langfuse - pipeline reliability decoupled from observability uptime.

43
00:09:04,286 --> 00:09:17,143
Tier-up routing - gpt-4o-mini default; tier up to gpt-4o on low-confidence high-stakes.

44
00:09:17,143 --> 00:09:30,000
HITL gate - pauses publication when score < threshold or any gap is low-confidence.

45
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,333
Headline numbers:

46
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:36,667
22 source documents - 14 regulatory PDFs + 8 policies.

47
00:09:36,667 --> 00:09:40,000
3 specialized agents over a 12-stage pipeline.

48
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,333
~700 LLM calls per full assessment for under $0.10.

49
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:46,667
< 30 minutes from raw PDFs to audit-ready DOCX.

50
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:50,000
100% LLM call coverage in Langfuse traces.

51
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,667
Recap.

52
00:09:51,667 --> 00:09:53,333
Layered, typed, observable Python system - not a notebook.

53
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:55,000
Three LCEL agents + RAG + NetworkX KG + deterministic scoring.

54
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,667
Audit-grade observability + resilience + HITL gate baked in.

55
00:09:56,667 --> 00:09:58,333
Three reach surfaces: CLI, Gradio dashboard, FastAPI.

56
00:09:58,333 --> 00:10:00,000
Thank you - questions welcome.
